# Core architecture

Permanent authority separation:

```text
PLANNER → proposes
VALIDATOR → evaluates
APPROVER → authorizes
EXECUTOR → acts
VERIFIER → measures
MEMORY → stores governed precedents
```

The Control Plane is configuration authority only. It does not execute.

Identity, permissions, state transitions, hashes, policies, budgets, approval binding, and execution authority must remain deterministic.

AI may determine what could be useful. Deterministic systems determine what is true, permitted, affordable, authorized, executable, successful, and worthy of being remembered.

Fail closed when authority is missing. Do not infer permissions. Do not add LLM, GitHub, or other external integrations unless the current milestone explicitly requires them.
